  ('dawurokese', 'Dawurokese Festival', 63, '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'published', null, 'oti', 'heritage', 'Kadjebi', 'Akan (Kadjebi)', '', 'The traditional festival of the people of Kadjebi, held in remembrance of the ancestors and to bring the people together.', '', 'detailed', false, '{"alternateNames":["Dawuro Kese"],"otherRegions":[],"traditionalArea":"Kadjebi","usualDate":"Every three years","duration":"","historicalSignificance":"After the people settled near Mount Kera, an epidemic reduced their numbers and enemies harassed them. Their chief, Nana Akompi, consulted an oracle and had a great gong, the \"dawurokese\", made; it was said to demoralise the enemy.","culturalSignificance":"The yearly spiritual and physical cleansing has become a call to protect the forest and streams.","activities":["Women sweep the town with a special leaf, shouting to drive away sickness"],"attractionsNearby":["Stone cave, Bakpa-Papase","Obuletey Cave, Asato"],"imageCredit":"","sources":["https://ghanaculture.gov.gh/oti-region/"],"notes":""}'::jsonb),
